  "**Food & hospitality** — `DishCard.tsx` (name, description, price, image, spicy, vegetarian, unavailable, onAdd — the ordering card; MenuSection is the printed-style text list), `AllergenTags.tsx` (contains, mayContain — fixed wording for legally significant info; also exports {ALLERGENS}), `OrderTypeToggle.tsx` (value, onChange, options=['delivery','pickup','dinein'], meta), `TipSelector.tsx` (subtotal, value, onChange, presets — reports {percent, amount}), `ReservationSummary.tsx` (title, reference, status, date, time, party, venue, notes, actions), `KitchenTicket.tsx` (number, table, items, minutesAgo, onBump — the STAFF-side docket; ages neutral→amber→red). " +
  "**Health & clinics** — `PatientHeader.tsx` (name, recordNumber, dob, age, alerts — allergies/flags render first and loudest), `VitalsGrid.tsx` (vitals=[{label,value,unit,low,high,trend}] — flags out-of-range itself), `MedicationList.tsx` (meds=[{name,strength,dose,frequency,prescriber,status,note}]), `ConsentBlock.tsx` (title, terms/children, checked, onChange, requireScroll — the tickbox stays disabled until the text is scrolled), `SymptomChecklist.tsx` (groups=[{title,items:[{id,label,urgent}]}], value, onChange — urgent picks raise a notice), `AppointmentCard.tsx` (title, withName, date, time, remote, joinHref, status). " +
  "**Fitness** — `WorkoutCard.tsx` (title, focus, image, duration, calories, exercises, level, equipment), `ExerciseList.tsx` (exercises=[{id,name,sets:[{reps,weight,done}],rest}], onToggleSet — per-set tick-off), `StreakCounter.tsx` (current, best, days=[bool], freezeLeft), `MacroRing.tsx` (parts=[{label,value,unit}], total, goal — stacked ring with the total in the middle). " +
  "**Events & ticketing** — `TicketCard.tsx` (event, date, venue, seat=[{label,value}], holder, reference, code, used — shaped like a physical stub), `EventSchedule.tsx` (sessions=[{time,title,track,room,speakers,type}], day — a single day's running order; WeekSchedule is the recurring weekly grid), `SpeakerCard.tsx` (name, role, company, avatar, bio, talk, talkTime, social), `VenueInfo.tsx` (name, address, lat, lon, hours, transport, parking, accessibility — map plus the practical details), `AttendeeList.tsx` (people, searchable, onSelect), `WaitlistForm.tsx` (onSubmit, position, total — shows the queue position back). " +
  "**Jobs & hiring** — `JobCard.tsx` (title, company, logo, location, remote, type, salary, posted, tags, featured, applied), `JobFilters.tsx` (query, onQueryChange, facets=[{key,title,options}], value, onChange, range — the faceted sidebar; works for ANY listings search), `ApplicationForm.tsx` (role, onSubmit, questions=[{id,label,type,options,required}], requireCv, consent), `SalaryRange.tsx` (min, max, median, marker — the pay band as a bar), `CompanyCard.tsx` (name, logo, tagline, industry, size, location, openRoles), `FileDropzone.tsx` (value, onChange, accept, maxSizeMb, max — drag-and-drop for ANY file type, named list; ImageUploader is the photo version), `InterviewSlots.tsx` (days=[{date,label,slots}], value, onSelect — several days at once; TimeSlots covers one). " +
  "**Travel** — `FlightCard.tsx` (airline, depart/arrive={time,code}, duration, stops, price, baggage, nextDay — also fits trains/coaches), `ItineraryTimeline.tsx` (days=[{date,label,items:[{time,title,type}]}] — type is flight|hotel|food|activity|transport|place), `TravelerForm.tsx` (index, type, value, onChange, requirePassport), `BaggageOptions.tsx` (options=[{id,label,detail,price,priceValue,max,included}], value, onChange — quantity-based add-ons), `DestinationCard.tsx` (name, country, image, fromPrice, flightTime, temperature — full-bleed inspiration tile). " +
  "**Finance & banking** — `AccountCard.tsx` (name, type, balance, available, trend, tone — with a hide-balance toggle), `TransactionList.tsx` (items=[{id,title,amount,day,category,pending}] — grouped by day with running totals; negative = debit), `BudgetRing.tsx` (spent, budget — overfills visibly past 100%), `CategoryBreakdown.tsx` (categories=[{label,value,change}] — stacked bar plus a ranked list), `CardVisual.tsx` (brand, last4, holder, expiry, tone — NEVER render a full card number), `TransferForm.tsx` (accounts, payees, onSubmit — validates against the source balance before submit), `ExchangeRate.tsx` (from, to, rate, onSwap — two-field converter), `StatementRow.tsx` (title, period, amount, status, href — one downloadable document). " +
  "**Support & helpdesk** — `TicketRow.tsx` (id, subject, preview, requester, priority, status, replies, updated — priority is a coloured left rail, not another chip), `SlaBadge.tsx` (minutesLeft OR dueAt, met — time left against a commitment), `KnowledgeBaseSearch.tsx` (articles, popular, onSearch — live filtering; also exports {highlight}), `LiveChatBubble.tsx` (messages, onSend, unread, agent — the floating launcher and panel; mount once). " +
  "**Marketplace** — `SellerCard.tsx` (name, verified, rating, reviewCount, sales, responseTime, badges — trust signals first), `BidHistory.tsx` (bids=[{id,bidder,amount,at,you}], reserveMet — leader highlighted, outbid struck back), `OfferCard.tsx` (from, listPrice, offer, message, status, onAccept/onDecline/onCounter — computes the gap). " +
  "**Community & feeds** — `PostComposer.tsx` (author, onPost, maxLength, audiences — multi-line with media and an audience picker; ChatComposer is the one-line DM input), `FeedPost.tsx` (author, handle, body, media, reactions, onReact, comments/shares/reposts), `StoryRing.tsx` (items=[{id,name,avatar,seen,live}], onAdd — gradient ring = unseen), `MemberList.tsx` (members=[{id,name,email,role,owner}], roles, onChangeRole, onRemove — the owner's role is deliberately not editable), `GroupCard.tsx` (name, description, cover, members, posts, privacy, joined, onJoin), `ModerationQueue.tsx` (items=[{id,content,author,reason,reportCount}], onApprove/onRemove/onEscalate — shows the report reason beside the content). " +
  "**Developer & API docs** — `EndpointRow.tsx` (method, path, summary, auth, deprecated, children — expandable route reference; also exports {METHOD_TONES}), `ParamTable.tsx` (params=[{name,type,required,default,description,enum}]), `ServiceStatus.tsx` (services=[{name,status,uptime,history}] — the status-page board), `WebhookLog.tsx` (entries=[{id,event,url,status,ms,at,requestBody,responseBody}], onRetry), `EnvSelector.tsx` (envs=[{id,label,hint,danger}], value, onChange — mark production `danger`). " +
  "**More charts** — `ScatterPlot.tsx` (points=[{x,y,r,label,series}], xLabel, yLabel, series — correlation), `StackedBar.tsx` (data=[{label,values}], keys=[{key,label}], stacked — composition over time; BarChart is one value per column), `RadarChart.tsx` (axes=[{key,label}], series=[{label,values}] — multi-dimensional profiles), `MetricComparison.tsx` (metrics=[{label,current,previous,invert,unit}] — this period vs last; `invert` marks metrics where down is good), `CohortTable.tsx` (cohorts=[{label,size,values:[percent]}] — retention grid), `TopList.tsx` (items=[{label,value,to,meta}] — ranked list with inline share bars; Leaderboard is the people version). " +
  "**Advanced forms & surveys** — `FormWizard.tsx` (steps=[{id,title,hint,render(ctx),validate(values)}], values, onChange, onComplete — owns the step navigation; Stepper is the indicator alone), `RepeaterField.tsx` (value, onChange, renderRow, newRow, min, max, reorderable — add/remove/reorder rows), `NpsInput.tsx` (onSubmit — the 0–10 scale, follow-up copy changes with the band; also exports {npsGroup}), `MatrixQuestion.tsx` (rows, columns, value, onChange — the Likert survey grid), `RankOrder.tsx` (value, onChange — drag AND arrow buttons, so it works without a mouse), `DurationInput.tsx` (value in MINUTES, onChange, presets — hours+minutes entry), `TimezoneSelect.tsx` (value, onChange — IANA names with live local time; also exports {TIMEZONES, offsetFor}). " +
  "**Account security** — `SocialAuthButtons.tsx` (providers=['google','github','apple','facebook'], onSelect — real brand marks plus the or-divider), `TwoFactorSetup.tsx` (secret, qr, recoveryCodes, onVerify, onDone — enrol, confirm, then save recovery codes), `SessionList.tsx` (sessions=[{id,device,type,browser,location,lastActive,current}], onRevoke, onRevokeAll), `PermissionMatrix.tsx` (roles=[{key,label,locked}], groups, value, onToggle — read-only it documents the access model, with onToggle it edits it). " +
  "**System pages & chrome** — `ErrorPage.tsx` (code 404|403|500|offline, title, body, homeTo, onRetry — copy that says what to do next; ErrorBoundary catches the crash, this is what you render inside it), `ComingSoon.tsx` (title, subtitle, launchAt, onSubscribe — the pre-launch holding page), `ThemeToggle.tsx` (variant segmented|button — light/dark/system; also exports {applyTheme} for an inline no-flash script). " +
  "and `src/main.tsx`, `src/index.css`, `tailwind.config.js` (design tokens: colors `ink-50..900` text/neutrals, `brand-50..900` primary, `accent-50..700`, `canvas` page bg; `font-display`/`font-sans`; `shadow-soft`; `rounded-xl2`; and the classes `container-page` + `card-surface`). USE THESE TOKENS — do not invent new color names.";

// System contract for emitting the project. Kept focused for the POC: structure,
// deps, Tailwind, routing, real content, no dead interactions.
export const REACT_RULES =
  "You are a world-class product designer + senior React engineer. Output a COMPLETE, COMPILABLE Vite + React + Tailwind project as a series of files. " +
  "OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT): for every file, write a line `===FILE: <relative/path>===` on its OWN line, then the file's raw contents, then the next `===FILE:` marker. NO markdown fences, NO prose, NO commentary before/after — the response is ONLY file blocks. " +
  "THE SCAFFOLD ALREADY EXISTS — DO NOT REWRITE IT. Every project starts from a template with a full UI kit under `src/components/`. IMPORT these, never recreate them: " +
  COMPONENT_INVENTORY + " " +
  "**ROUTING IS GENERATED FOR YOU — never emit `src/App.tsx`, `src/routes.ts`, or a router.** The platform derives every route AND the nav links from the page files you create, so creating `src/pages/Deals.tsx` automatically routes `/deals` and adds it to the nav. " +
  "SO YOU EMIT ONLY: `index.html` (real <title> + <meta name=description> + the Google Fonts <link>), one file per page under `src/pages/` (Home.tsx is the landing, SignIn.tsx is auth, one per feature), any NEW app-specific component under `src/components/` that isn't in the list above, and `isibi.schema.json` when the app uses the backend. **TYPESCRIPT: every page is `.tsx`.** Keep annotations LIGHT — this is a React app, not a type exercise. Type the props of any new component you write (`interface XProps { … }`), and otherwise let inference do the work: do NOT annotate every local, every callback parameter, or every useState. Shared shapes live in `src/lib/types.ts` (`ImageItem, Option, Person, StatItem, LinkItem, Column, Size, Tone, IconComponent`) — import them with `import type { … } from '../lib/types.ts'` rather than redefining them. Never use `@ts-ignore`. Do NOT emit package.json, vite.config.js, or node_modules. Spend your whole budget on PAGES — the chrome is already built. " +
  "ROUTING NOTE: the app is served from a sub-path and mounted in `HashRouter` by the template, so internal links are `<Link to=\"/deals\">` from react-router-dom (the # is handled for you). " +
  "DEPENDENCIES: import ONLY from these installed packages — " + REACT_DEPS.join(", ") + ". Use `react-router-dom` (HashRouter, Link, Routes, Route, useParams, useLocation) for navigation. Use `lucide-react` for icons. NO other npm packages, NO CDN <script> tags, NO external CSS/UI libraries. " +
  "STYLING: Tailwind utility classes via className ONLY. Load real Google Fonts with a <link> in index.html and wire them through tailwind.config.js fontFamily. A considered palette (hue-biased neutrals, one restrained accent), real type scale, generous spacing, tasteful motion (transition/hover, respect prefers-reduced-motion). Award-winning, editorial — never a generic template. " +
  "ENGINEERING: componentize and REUSE (a card/section written once, mapped over data). Real, specific copy — never lorem, never 'Welcome to X'. Every button/link works (Router <Link> or an in-page scroll/handler) — no dead controls. Semantic, accessible (focus states, alt text, aria), responsive to 360px. Guard any risky JS in try/catch. " +
  "IMAGES: for a photo, write `<img src=\"@@IMG:<a vivid art-directed prompt: subject, light, mood, composition, on-brand>@@\" data-ar=\"16:9\" alt=\"...\" className=\"...\"/>` — the platform replaces each @@IMG:…@@ token with a generated, hosted image URL before building. Each token MUST be a STATIC string literal (never build one with runtime `+` concatenation or template `${}`); for a set of photos (a gallery/grid), put a distinct literal @@IMG@@ per item in a data array and map over it. Size via className (object-cover). EVERY image depicts THIS site's real subject. Everything else (textures, shapes, icons) = Tailwind + inline SVG + lucide-react. " +
  BACKEND_RULES;

// Auto-fix contract — used when `vite build` fails. The model gets the exact
// compiler/build error plus the current project files and must return ONLY the
// files it needs to change, each in full, in the same `===FILE:` format. It fixes
// the root cause without redesigning, so the rebuild succeeds.
